{
  "date": "2026-10-13",
  "title": "Who Are You Becoming to Belong?",
  "tagline": "If belonging requires you to repeatedly betray conviction, the price of admission is becoming too expensive.",
  "series": "The Battle Before the Battle",
  "seo_title": "Becoming Someone Else to Belong | TheWrkShop",
  "seo_description": "Sometimes the room doesn’t ask you to deny Christ. It trains you to edit Him out. On belonging, conformity and integrity in every setting.",
  "og_image": "/assets/og/who-are-you-becoming-to-belong.png",
  "scriptures": [
    {
      "ref": "Galatians 2:12",
      "text": "“When they arrived, he began to draw back and separate himself from the Gentiles because he was afraid….”"
    },
    {
      "ref": "Romans 12:2",
      "text": "“Do not conform to the pattern of this world, but be transformed by the renewing of your mind.”"
    }
  ],
  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "the_revelation",
      "label": "The Revelation",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Most people don’t walk into a room thinking:"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "“TODAY I WILL COMPROMISE WHO I AM.”"
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "It happens more quietly.",
            "You observe.",
            "Adjust.",
            "Learn the language.",
            "Notice what gets rewarded.",
            "Notice what gets punished."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Then slowly:"
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "you become fluent in the room.",
            "Different jokes.",
            "Different vocabulary.",
            "Different convictions.",
            "Different courage.",
            "Different version of you.",
            "Church you.",
            "Work you.",
            "Guys’-night you.",
            "Online you.",
            "Leadership you.",
            "Home you."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "And eventually we have to ask:"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "WHICH ONE IS ACTUALLY YOU?"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "the_lie",
      "label": "The Lie",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "“I’M JUST READING THE ROOM.”"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Sometimes that’s wisdom."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Paul adapted culturally for the sake of the gospel."
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Jesus interacted differently with different people.",
            "Maturity requires situational awareness."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "But adaptation becomes compromise when:"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "THE ROOM DOESN’T MERELY CHANGE HOW I COMMUNICATE."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "IT CHANGES WHAT I’M WILLING TO OBEY."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "That’s different."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "the_truth",
      "label": "The Truth",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Romans 12 warns:"
        },
        {
          "type": "quote",
          "text": "“Do not conform….”"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Conformity is powerful because it often happens gradually."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Nobody announces:"
        },
        {
          "type": "quote",
          "text": "“Become like us.”"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Instead:"
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "laugh here.",
            "stay quiet there.",
            "don’t mention that.",
            "wear this.",
            "admire these people.",
            "desire these things.",
            "hide those struggles.",
            "Then belonging begins shaping identity."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "SOMETIMES THE ROOM DOESN’T ASK YOU TO DENY CHRIST."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "IT JUST TRAINS YOU TO EDIT HIM OUT."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "That’s much subtler."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "the_belonging_battle",
      "label": "The Belonging Battle",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Watch the progression:"
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Enter room.",
            "↓",
            "Read expectations.",
            "↓",
            "Detect belonging requirements.",
            "↓",
            "Anticipate rejection.",
            "↓",
            "Edit self.",
            "↓",
            "Receive acceptance.",
            "↓",
            "Editing gets rewarded.",
            "↓",
            "Edited version becomes easier.",
            "Now something serious is happening."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "BELONGING HAS BECOME FORMATIONAL."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "but_dont_confuse_integrity_with_sameness",
      "label": "But Don’t Confuse Integrity With Sameness",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Integrity doesn’t mean behaving identically in every environment."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "You speak differently in a boardroom than with your children."
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Different relationships reveal different parts of personality.",
            "That’s normal."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The issue is:"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "DOES THE SAME LORD GOVERN EVERY VERSION OF ME?"
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Same integrity.",
            "Same holiness.",
            "Same allegiance.",
            "Same fundamental character.",
            "Different setting.",
            "Same Lord."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "jesus_wasnt_controlled_by_the_room",
      "label": "Jesus Wasn’t Controlled by the Room",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Jesus could enter:"
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "synagogues.",
            "homes.",
            "crowds.",
            "dinners with sinners.",
            "religious gatherings.",
            "Roman spaces.",
            "And the room never became His lord.",
            "He could love without conforming.",
            "Listen without surrendering truth.",
            "Enter without becoming.",
            "Engage without being absorbed.",
            "That’s freedom."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "JESUS COULD ENTER THE ROOM WITHOUT NEEDING THE ROOM TO TELL HIM WHO HE WAS."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "And because our identity is increasingly rooted in Him, we can learn the same freedom."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "the_audit",
      "label": "The Audit",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullet_list",
          "items": [
            "WHERE DO I BECOME A DIFFERENT VERSION OF MYSELF?",
            "WHAT DO I EDIT?"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "My convictions?",
            "Language?",
            "Marriage?",
            "Faith?",
            "Purity?",
            "Honesty?",
            "Humility?"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "WHAT AM I TRYING TO PRESERVE?"
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Approval?",
            "Opportunity?",
            "Status?",
            "Belonging?"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Then ask:"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "WHAT IS BELONGING COSTING ME?"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "the_surrender",
      "label": "The Surrender",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Before entering an influential room, decide:"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "“JESUS IS ALREADY LORD HERE.”"
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "I don’t need to perform.",
            "I don’t need to prove."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "I don’t need to become difficult or obnoxious."
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "I can listen.",
            "Learn.",
            "Adapt.",
            "Love."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "But:"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "I WILL NOT RENT MY IDENTITY TO THE ROOM."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "take_it_with_you",
      "label": "Take It With You",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "quote",
          "text": "Does the same Lord govern every version of me?"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "the_prayer",
      "label": "The Prayer",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Father,",
            "Show me where belonging has been shaping me more than I realized."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Expose the places where I edit obedience to preserve acceptance."
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Give me wisdom to adapt without compromising.",
            "Love without conforming.",
            "Listen without losing conviction."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Root my identity so deeply in Christ that I can enter any room without needing that room to tell me who I am."
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Jesus,",
            "be Lord of every version of me."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "In Jesus name,",
            "Amen."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "hidden_gems",
      "label": "Hidden Gems 💎",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "If belonging requires you to repeatedly betray conviction, the price of admission is becoming too expensive."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "💎",
          "text": "Sometimes the room doesn’t ask you to deny Christ. It just trains you to edit Him out."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "💎",
          "text": "Belonging can become formational."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "💎",
          "text": "Does the same Lord govern every version of me?"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "💎",
          "text": "Jesus could enter the room without needing the room to tell Him who He was."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "💎",
          "text": "I will not rent my identity to the room."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "-TheWrkShop"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
